The output of mm_mul rewritten with pat2.pat must match clang -O0 on the original
source. The timing line differs between runs, so it is left out.

RUN: clang -O0 %S/extr_matmul_c.c_mm_mul.c -o %t.ref
RUN: %t.ref | grep -v Tempo > %t.ref.out
RUN: smr %S/extr_matmul_c.c_mm_mul.c %S/pat2.pat -o %t.mlir
RUN: cir-translate --cir-to-llvmir %t.mlir -o %t.ll
RUN: clang %t.ll -lopenblas -lpthread -lm -o %t.bin
RUN: %t.bin | grep -v Tempo > %t.out
RUN: diff %t.ref.out %t.out

The dot product loop that replaces the inner loop of mm_mul is unrolled by 4,
then followed by the loop for the leftover iterations.

RUN: FileCheck %s --input-file=%t.mlir

CHECK-LABEL: cir.func {{.*}}@mm_mul(
CHECK:         cir.for : cond {
CHECK:         } body {
CHECK-COUNT-4:   cir.binop(mul, {{.*}}) : !cir.double
CHECK-NOT:       cir.binop(mul
CHECK:         } step {
CHECK:         cir.for : cond {
CHECK:         } body {
CHECK-COUNT-1:   cir.binop(mul, {{.*}}) : !cir.double
CHECK:         } step {
